  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Monitoring and Evaluation of CARA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MEL seeks to help measure and track the progress of CARA programmes toward its intended outcome/s; demonstrate the status of an activity, project, or program. It helps maximise the programme&#x2019;s Value for Money (4E&#x2019;s) which include Economy, Effectiveness, Efficiency and Equity and sustainability of impact. Also, it helps strengthen the global evidence base on climate adaptation and resilience programming by providing new and quality evidence on what works and what does not work for building adaptation and resilience to climate change. Ensure rigorous monitoring, evaluation and learning (MEL) approaches  to improve performance management, accountability, and evidence-based decision making.</narrative>
  </description>
